# Pipeline run outputs (per-episode working directory).
# These are large binary outputs from real recording sessions and personal
# audio content — must never reach a public AGPL repo. Added 2026-05-04
# after the 0788a53 incident where auto-backup committed 5+ GB of WAVs.
working/
contextpulse_pipeline/examples/ep-*/

# Internal handoff / resumption docs. Added 2026-08-17: an auto-backup commit
# (ab50edc, 2026-04-27) put HANDOFF_PHASE3_AMI_BAKE_2026-04-27.md at repo root,
# and it references ~/Projects/CryptoTrader/ — a different private venture — in
# a PUBLIC repo. Size guards can't see a 13 KB text file and gitleaks hunts
# secrets, not other projects' names, so nothing caught it.
HANDOFF_*.md
RESUMPTION_*.md

# Podcast / multi-source audio pipeline — LOCAL ONLY (David, 2026-08-17).
# Untracked from git on 2026-08-17; the files remain on disk. This is personal
# recording work (DJI mics, named participants, listen-test labels) and is not
# part of the open-core product. May move to a private repo later.
#
# History: the 2026-05-04 rule above only covered contextpulse_pipeline/examples/,
# while the package itself had been tracked since 2026-04-26 — eight days earlier —
# and .gitignore never untracks what is already tracked. That gap is why a merge
# audit found 12 files carrying hardcoded C:\Users\david paths bound for a public
# repo. The rules below only hold because the files were untracked first.
contextpulse_pipeline/

# Pipeline scripts (same effort, live in scripts/ alongside legitimate tooling,
